<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Świętopełk II, Duke of Pomerania</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1195–<a href="/years/1266">1266</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Świętopełk II the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Świętopełk II the Great (c. 1195–1266) was Duke of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pomerelia">Pomerelia</a>, the most powerful of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samborides">Samborides</a>. In 1227 he threw off Polish overlordship and was involved in the killing of the Polish high duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leszek-the-white">Leszek the White</a> at Gąsawa. He later fought long wars against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/teutonic-order">Teutonic Order</a>, at times in alliance with the pagan Prussians.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swietopelk-ii-duke-of-pomerania.jpg" alt="Świętopełk II, Duke of Pomerania" width="320" height="726" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Herman Han (1574-1627) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Swantopolk_II,_Duke_of_Pomerania.PNG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
